The code in both `kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable` and `kvm_s390_pci_aif_disable` contains the vulnerable construct:


gaite = (struct zpci_gaite *)aift->gait + (zdev->aisb * sizeof(struct zpci_gaite));


This performs double-scaling pointer arithmetic: casting `aift->gait` to a `struct zpci_gaite *` already scales additions by `sizeof(struct zpci_gaite)`, but the code explicitly multiplies the index by that size as well. This leads to an out-of-bounds access when `zdev->aisb` is large. The fix (removing the explicit multiplication) is not present in this commit.
